Gate readcon-core 0.17.1's C API behind its `capi` feature and make `capi` a
default feature, so a consumer that disables default features (readcon-db 0.2.0
with readcon-db-production.diff) links the Rust API without exporting any rkr_*
symbol, while any consumer using the defaults keeps the C API it had.

Provider repair candidate readcon-core-default-capi.diff (sha256
3f30ce94c0dd7ad96d0cb5e42c15b9f632a47894a9d5cf6d95e9f4b9b60221d3), written
against readcon-core v0.17.1 (6993e306). The src/ hunks below are verbatim. The
crates.io crate (sha256 c8c9ec4a...) ships the cargo-normalized Cargo.toml, with
the git manifest as Cargo.toml.orig, so the Cargo.toml hunk makes the same
change (default = [] -> default = ["capi"]) in the published manifest.
Applied in the vendored crate: sourcepath ../easybuild_vendor/readcon-core-0.17.1.

